      "name": "Kamakurakokomae Station",
      "description": "Kamakurakōkōmae Station (Japanese: 鎌倉高校前駅, Hepburn: Kamakurakōkōmae-eki; lit. 'Kamakura High School Station') is a railway station on the Enoshima Electric Railway (Enoden), located in the Koshigoe neighborhood of Kamakura, Kanagawa, Japan. Though small in size, it is known for its scenery, as it commands an open view of the Pacific Ocean and Mount Fuji from the station platform.",
